    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="75.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 75.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="75.1" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="362" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ se ðe þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> wæpn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IICn_75-1.lnote.oe.13"/> áge, hine geladige, gif he durre, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> hit næfre næs naðer ne his gewill<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IICn_75-1.lnote.oe.14"/> ne his geweald ne his ræd ne his gewitnes: þonne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#IICn_75-1.lnote.oe.15"/> is þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> Godes riht, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he beo clæne.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#IICn_75-1.lnote.oe.16"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="75.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="362" ed="#liebermann"/>And se ðe þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> wepn age, hine geladige, gyf he durre, ðæt hit næfre næs naðer ne his gewill ne his geweald ne his ræd ne his gewitnes: ðonne is þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> Godes riht, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> heo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_75-1.lnote.oe.4"/> beo clæne.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="75.1" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="362" ed="#liebermann"/>And se ðe þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> wæpen age, hine geladige, gif he durre, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> hit næffre<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_75-1.lnote.oe.2"/> næs naðer ne his gewyll ne his geweald ne his ræd ne his gewitnes: þonne his<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_75-1.lnote.oe.2"/> þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> Godes riht, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he beo clæne.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="75.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="363" ed="#liebermann"/>Et si<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_75-1.lnote.oe.6"/> ille, cuius armis malefactum est, se adlegiare audeat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_75-1.lnote.oe.7"/>, quod nec uelle nec<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_75-1.lnote.oe.8"/> (uel) posse suum fuerit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IICn_75-1.lnote.oe.9-2"/> nec<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_75-1.lnote.oe.8"/> (uel) testimonium<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_75-1.lnote.oe.10-2"/>, Dei rectum est, ut inde quietus sit.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="75.1" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="363" ed="#liebermann"/>Et ille qui lanceam posuit, ubi sine lesione iacere<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_75-1.lnote.oe.7-2"/> potuisset, si dimitteretur, purget se, si audet, quod non fuit eius uoluntate nec potestate nec consilio nec<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_75-1.lnote.oe.8-2"/> testimonio eius malum factum quod actum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IICn_75-1.lnote.oe.9-3"/> est: erit tunc rectum secundum iusticiam, ut ipse sit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_75-1.lnote.oe.10-3"/> inculpabilis.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="75.1" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="363" ed="#liebermann"/>[75, 1] si armature possessor inficiari (uoluerit) possit, illud malefactum nec sua uoluntate nec sua potestate nec suo consilio nec sua conscientia fuisse patratum, iustum secundum Deum censeo, armature possessorem esse innocentem,</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="75.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="212" ed="#robertson"/>And se ðe þæt wepn age, hine geladige, gyf he durre, ðæt hit næfre næs naðer ne his gewill ne his geweald ne his ræd ne his gewitnes; ðonne is þæt Godes riht, þæt he<ptr type="editorNote" n="10" target="#IICn_75-1.robnote.fn.10"/> beo clæne.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="292" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And se ðe þæt wæpn age, hine geladige, gif he durre, þæt hit næfre næs naðer ne his gewill ne his geweald ne his ræd ne his gewitnes; þonne is þæt Godes riht þæt he beo clæne.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="362" ed="#liebermann"/>Und wer die Waffe zu eigen hat, reinige sich, wenn er es wagt [durch dén Eid<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_75-1.lnote.de.1"/>], dass es [das Verbrechen] nimmer weder sein Wille, noch seine Absicht, noch sein Rath, noch sein Mitwissen war: dann ist es Gottes [<hi rend="italic">d. h</hi>. vollkommenes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_75-1.lnote.de.2"/>] Recht, dass er rein dastehe.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And whoever owns the weapon, let him clear himself, if he dares, [by the oath] that it [the crime] was never either his will, nor his intention, nor his counsel, nor his knowledge: then it is God's [that is, perfect] right that he stand clean.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="213" ed="#robertson"/>And he who owns the weapon shall clear himself, if he dare, asserting that the mischief was done without his desire or authority or advice or cognisance; then according to the law of God he shall be clear [of any charge of complicity].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="473" ed="#whitelock"/>And he who owns the weapon is to clear himself, if he dare, that it was never either his wish or his intention or his advice or his cognisance; then it is the law of God that he should be clear.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="293" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And the weapon’s owner shall, if he dares, swear an oath of exculpation that he had neither intention nor authority nor complicity nor awareness concerning the crime; then by God’s law he shall be considered innocent.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 363, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_75-1.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">363</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">uo. <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi>; po. <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">uo. Hk; po. Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_75-1.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">363</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">i. s. D. c. <hi rend="italic">fehlt Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">i. s. D. c. lacking in Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_75-1.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">362</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_75-1.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">363</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cuius arma fuerant, emundet se <hi rend="italic">Hn</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cuius arma fuerant, emundet se Hn</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_75-1.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">363</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">uelit <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">uelit K</seg></note>
